  "goodToKnow": "Das Teleskop is a telescope; the native word is das Fernrohr. Germany's Effelsberg radio telescope in the Eifel, with a 100-metre dish, was the world's largest fully steerable radio telescope for decades. Die Sternwarte is an observatory, and many towns have public ones. Teleskopartig means telescopic: ein Teleskopstiel (extendable handle). Plural: die Teleskope."
